  "//": [
    "DO NOT EDIT MANUALLY. Regenerate with `node .githooks/update-deadcode-baseline.mjs`.",
    "",
    "Every entry is a Go function `deadcode ./...` reports unreachable from main()",
    "on this machine. It may only shrink. A function deadcode reports that is not",
    "listed here is a new violation and fails the pre-commit hook.",
    "",
    "Machine-specific in one respect: build-tag-gated files (e.g.",
    "secretservice_linux.go) only appear on the OS they build for, so an entry",
    "that vanishes on another platform is a free shrink, not a violation.",
    "",
    "That cuts both ways, and only one direction was written down. The twin the",
    "other OS compiles is a *new* file path, so the first run on that OS reports",
    "it as a new violation rather than a free shrink. A per-OS pair therefore",
    "needs BOTH halves listed, and this file is the union across the platforms",
    "the gate runs on, not a snapshot of whichever one generated it. The update",
    "script cannot do this for you: it sees one OS at a time, so the half it did",
    "not compile looks like a shrink and it removes it.",
    "",
    "Two entries were added BY HAND on 2026-08-06 (nocx-708q), which the update",
    "script refuses to do for you on purpose. Both are reasoned, not overlooked:",
    "",
    "  openability.go CanExpand \u2014 the expand half of the spec table. Its only",
